---
/**
 * The /writing headline (docs/projects/redesign/design-export/README.md §3).
 *
 * The same hero shape as every other page — H1, then a statement beside a
 * bordered right-hand block — with the fill in WRITING BLUE. The spec's rule is
 * that the fill always takes the colour of the section it belongs to, which is
 * why `.rd-fill` (global.css) is parameterised rather than hard-coded to
 * magenta.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE AND LAYOUT ARE `.rd-hero` IN global.css: the H1, the 32ch
 * lede, the row, the right block's hairline shell and the 720px collapse. What
 * stays here is the subscribe block's own content and colours.
 *
 * RETRO RESTYLES THIS SAME MARKUP under
 * `html[data-appearance='retro'] [data-module='writing-hero']` in retro.css. The
 * module prefix there is what buys those rules the one extra attribute they
 * need to outweigh the Astro-scoped selectors below, whose
 * `[data-astro-cid-…]` counts as a class. Nothing here is appearance-aware.
 */
---

{/*
  A div, not a section. `npm run validate:html` names an h1 inside sectioning
  content ("Consider using the h1 element as a top-level heading only"), and an
  unnamed <section> is not exposed as a region anyway — so the element was
  carrying the warning and nothing else.
*/}
<div class="rd-section rd-hero writing-hero" data-module="writing-hero">
  <h1><span class="rd-fill rd-fill--writing">Writing</span></h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      Notes on accessibility, agents, and building a site that tells the truth about itself.
    </p>
    {/*
      The subscribe block. Two real endpoints, each in the colour of what it
      serves: the feed is a writing surface, /llms.txt is an agent surface.
    */}
    <div class="hero-aside hero-subscribe">
      <span class="hero-subscribe-copy">Subscribe or read it as data.</span>
      <span class="hero-subscribe-links">
        <a href="/rss.xml" class="link-writing">rss.xml</a>
        <a href="/llms.txt" class="link-agents">llms.txt</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .writing-hero { padding-top: 78px; }

  .hero-subscribe { gap: 10px; }

  .hero-subscribe-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-5);
  }

  .hero-subscribe-links {
    display: flex;
    column-gap: 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .link-writing { color: var(--writing); }
  .link-writing:hover { color: var(--writing-hover); }
  .link-agents { color: var(--agents); }
  .link-agents:hover { color: var(--agents-hover); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .writing-hero { padding-top: 40px; }

    /* 44px tap targets, per the mobile spec. */
    .hero-subscribe-links a {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 10px 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
